"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/deployments","created_at":"2015-04-13T18:04:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T14:39:15Z","pushed_at":"2026-10-29T14:39:07Z","git_url":"git://github.com/apache/airflow.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:apache/airflow.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow","homepage":"https://airflow.apache.org/","size":790917,"stargazers_count":47308,"watchers_count":47308,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":18214,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":1927,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["airflow","apache","apache-airflow","automation","dag","data-engineering","data-integration","data-orchestrator","data-pipelines","data-science","elt","etl","machine-learning","mlops","orchestration","python","scheduler","workflow","workflow-engine","workflow-orchestration"],"visibility":"public","forks":18214,"open_issues":1927,"watchers":47308,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls/71074","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/71074","diff_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/71074.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/71074.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-22T07:41:26Z"},"body":"closes: #71070\r\n\r\nTwo producer assets that emit events for the same partition at the same moment can each create a pending `AssetPartitionDagRun`. The events end up split across two rows, so a consumer scheduled on `asset_a & asset_b` waits forever. The old find-or-create locked the producer's `AssetModel` row, but two different producers lock two different rows.\r\n\r\nThis adds a unique constraint on `(target_dag_id, pending_partition_key)`. When two writers race, the second INSERT fails inside a savepoint and that writer reuses the row the first one created. If the scheduler already consumed that row before the loser re-selects, its key is released and the lookup finds nothing, so the loser INSERTs again (two attempts in total) instead of failing the task. #58919 already ruled out locking the Dag row, and an advisory lock would serialize unrelated Dags too. I added a test that drives two sessions through `register_asset_change` the way the race happens in production. It leaves two pending rows on main and one row with both events here, on Postgres and MySQL.\r\n\r\n`pending_partition_key` exists because MySQL has no partial unique index. It holds the partition key while the row is pending, and a `@validates` hook clears it when `created_dag_run_id` is set. Unique indexes treat NULLs as distinct on all three backends, so consumed rows never collide.\r\n\r\nSince #68517 made batching opt-in, a Dag without `batch_asset_events` is supposed to get one APDR per event. Those rows are written with a NULL pending key and the constraint ignores them. The reuse lookup still matches any pending row for the key, so a Dag that switches batching on keeps adding to its latest pending row.\r\n\r\nMigration `0148` (3.4.0) adds the column and the constraint, and sets `pending_partition_key` on the latest pending row of each (Dag, key). Older duplicate pending rows are left alone: a Dag without `batch_asset_events` legitimately has one row per event, and merging them would collapse several Dag runs into one. Their NULL key never collides with the constraint, and offline mode runs the same SQL. The 3.5.0 migration becomes `0149`, the same reshuffle #74837 did. A development database already at the old 3.5.0 head (`c71065a1b14f`) skips `0148`, so downgrade it past `0149` and upgrade again.\r\n\r\n### Known issues\r\n\r\nAn INSERT that hits another transaction's uncommitted row waits for it to finish. If two producer transactions each create new pending rows for the same two (Dag, key) pairs in opposite orders, they deadlock. Sorting target Dags by `dag_id` rules that out for the Dags of a single event. It can still happen across a task's outlets, or when two mappers emit the same keys in a different order. `ti_update_state` marks the task FAILED on an unexpected exception today, deadlocks included. I'll send a follow-up so a deadlock there returns a 5xx and the worker retries.\r\n\r\nThis needs to go to `v3-4-test` before 3.4.0 final, since the migration is stamped 3.4.0.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/71074/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/71074/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":29109250583,"node_id":"REFE_lADOAgUK288AAAABLYG-188AAAAGxwvqFw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/events/29109250583","actor":{"login":"anmolxlight","id":116251176,"node_id":"U_kgDOBu3aKA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/116251176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anmolxlight","html_url":"htt